Hello,

 In **datatables.js**, we do the following to edit a cell:

```js
            var valueNew = $input.val();
            if (valueNew != value) {
              _cell.data(valueNew);
```

But I've just realized that the new value is not a number anymore, it is a string. Because although `$input` is a number input, `$input.val()` returns a string.

I found a nice solution [here](https://stackoverflow.com/a/70143214/1100107):

```js
$.valHooks.number = {
  get: function( elem ) {
    return elem.value * 1;
  }
};
```
If you agree, I do a PR to include this code (but at which location of the code should we include it?).

